      "message": "fix(app,motion): judge probe and plasma on a reduced-fidelity model; the cone and engrave rides stay refused for a stated reason\n\nProbe's protected-move law (ball distance and stem/body solid law) and\nplasma's kerf and cover laws give a coarse model's excess back out of\ntheir slack while a positive slack is left (the #864 rule); past that\nthe program gate refuses the operation by name. Both kinds leave the\nrefused list in fidelity_law::excess_aware, and floor_of lists their\nown slacks.\n\nThe cone and engrave rides stay refused: no tolerance holds the ride to\nthe model, so there is nothing to tighten (reason in fidelity_law's\nheader and docs/decisions/1053-fidelity-probe-plasma.md). The cross\ndrill stays refused: its standoff readings measure the mesh with no\nslack; that remainder keeps #1053 open.\n\nRefs #1053\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
